tifact (weight 1.0, no issue codes) is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). Even if it were, the deciding fact is carried independently by EV-TRIP-00717, so no confidence cap and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation follows.\n\nPOL-NS-06(i): EV-ADVIS-00717-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT). A missing advisory makes the interval-summing limb unavailable to either side and proves nothing against the driver; the rider-side claim asserting it against the driver was discarded at the citation stage for not naming the issue code.\n\nOn the chat and the pickup: EV-CHAT-00717 holds exactly one message, the driver's 14:12:40 note about the alternative entrance. POL-NS-04(a) fails (the rider sent no locating message) and POL-NS-03(i) is not reached (the rider named no entrance). The closest recorded approach, 297.70 m, sits inside the 300 m leash, so the pickup is a POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance question rather than a POL-NS-05 false-arrival one, and POL-NS-03 also refunds only the SGD 0.00 cancellation fee.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires: the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check reads no_show_terminations_30d 1 over completed_trips_30d 110 (rate 0.009) against the 4-and-0.08 test and does not trip, and no_show_disputes_30d and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nOutcome: the rider's claim is not supported. NO_ACTION — the fare stands exactly as charged: SGD 28.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00. No refund, no driver compensation, no referral."
